{
  "$schema": "https://app.kilo.ai/config.json",
  "commit_message": {
    "prompt": "Generate a concise Git commit message in French following Angular Conventional Commits and Semantic Versioning. Keep only the commit type in English. Use the format <type>(<scope>): <description>, where scope is optional. For breaking changes, use <type>(<scope>)!: <description> or <type>!: <description>. Use only these types: build, chore, ci, docs, feat, fix, perf, refactor, revert, style, test. Choose the type based on the actual diff: feat for new features (minor release), fix for bug fixes (patch release), perf for performance improvements (patch release), and ! for breaking changes (major release). Other types normally do not trigger a release. Conjugate French verbs in the third-person singular present indicative, as if the sentence started with 'Ce commit'. Never use infinitives. Prefer 'ajoute', 'corrige', 'modifie', 'supprime', 'améliore', 'met à jour' instead of 'ajouter', 'corriger', 'modifier', 'supprimer', 'améliorer', 'mettre à jour'. Keep the message short, precise, and limited to actual changes in the staged diff. Do not invent changes, add unnecessary explanations, use a period at the end, or capitalize the description after the colon. Prefer one clear sentence. Examples: feat(auth): ajoute la connexion avec OAuth; fix(api): corrige le bug des jetons expirés; docs: met à jour la documentation; refactor: simplifie la gestion des utilisateurs; feat!: publie un changement incompatible. Output only the commit message without Markdown formatting."
  }
}